==Icelandic==
===Etymology===
From {{etyl|non|is}} {{term|biðja|lang=non}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|is}} {{term/t|gem-pro|*bidjaną}}. Cognate with {{etyl|de|-}} {{term|bitten|lang=de}}, {{etyl|fo|-}} {{term|biðja|lang=fo}}, {{etyl|da|-}} {{term|bede|lang=da}}, {{etyl|sv|-}} {{term|bedja|lang=sv}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈpɪðja/|lang=is}}
*: {{rhymes|ɪðja|lang=is}}

===Verb===
{{is-verb-strong|bað|báðu|beðið}}
# {{context|ambitransitive|governs the accusative|optionally ditransitive with genitive|lang=is}} to [[ask]], [[request]] some action of someone
#: ''Ég '''bað''' þig nú bara um [[greiði|greiða]].''
#:: I just '''asked''' you a [[favour]].
# {{context|intransitive|lang=is}} to [[pray]]
#: ''Ég '''bið''' til [[Guð]]s.''
#:: I '''pray''' to [[God]].

